WEBVTT

00:00:10.498 --> 00:00:11.538
(CHUCKLES)

00:00:12.458 --> 00:00:15.098
YOUNG ELSA: Hi, I'm Olaf.
And I like warm hugs.

00:00:15.298 --> 00:00:17.378
YOUNG ANNA:
I love you, Olaf!

00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:18.458
(GIGGLING)

00:00:18.538 --> 00:00:20.378
IDUNA: Come on,
you can do it.

00:00:20.818 --> 00:00:23.058
-(SINGING) Here I stand
-Oh.

00:00:23.138 --> 00:00:24.178
In the light of day

00:00:24.258 --> 00:00:25.778
DUKE OF WESELTON:
Oh! Like a chicken

00:00:25.898 --> 00:00:27.338
with the face of a monkey!

00:00:27.418 --> 00:00:29.178
ANNA: I just wasn't looking
where I was going.

00:00:29.258 --> 00:00:30.778
But I'm great actually.

00:00:30.978 --> 00:00:33.178
HANS: Prince Hans
of the Southern Isles.

00:00:34.298 --> 00:00:35.298
AGNARR: I love you.

00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:37.018
I need to tell you
about my past.

00:00:37.098 --> 00:00:38.098
And where I'm from.

00:00:38.178 --> 00:00:39.378
I'm listening.

00:00:39.698 --> 00:00:41.658
-(YOUNG IDUNA GIGGLING)
-Iduna!

00:00:41.738 --> 00:00:43.258
What are you reading,
Your Majesty?

00:00:43.338 --> 00:00:44.578
Oh, some new Danish author.

00:00:45.258 --> 00:00:46.378
(GASPS)

00:00:47.818 --> 00:00:49.058
(CHITTERING)

00:00:52.058 --> 00:00:54.738
SOLDIER: King Runeard,
I'm sorry. I don't understand.

00:00:54.818 --> 00:00:55.818
Grandfather?

00:00:56.018 --> 00:00:58.058
We bring Arendelle's
full guard.

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:01.378
But they have given us
no reason not to trust them.

00:01:02.138 --> 00:01:03.738
The Northuldra follow magic.

00:01:03.818 --> 00:01:05.578
Which means
we can never trust them.

00:01:05.738 --> 00:01:06.738
Grandfather?

00:01:06.818 --> 00:01:10.018
Magic makes people feel
too powerful. Too entitled.

00:01:10.178 --> 00:01:14.298
It makes them think they can
defy the will of a king.

00:01:14.458 --> 00:01:16.258
That is not what magic does.

00:01:16.418 --> 00:01:17.778
That's just your fear.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.218
Fear is what can't be trusted.

00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:29.818
You see, the dam
will weaken their lands,

00:01:29.898 --> 00:01:31.458
so they will
have to turn to me.

00:01:33.578 --> 00:01:37.778
IDUNA: (SINGING)
Dive down deep into her sound

00:01:37.938 --> 00:01:42.578
But not too far,
or you'll be drowned

00:01:42.738 --> 00:01:44.818
RUNEARD: They will come
in celebration.

00:01:45.018 --> 00:01:48.418
And then, we will know
their size and strength.

00:01:50.258 --> 00:01:53.178
As you have welcomed us,
we welcome you...

00:01:53.538 --> 00:01:55.898
our neighbors, our friends.

00:02:01.138 --> 00:02:02.298
(GRUNTS)

00:02:02.378 --> 00:02:04.378
-(SHIVERING)
-(DEEP RUMBLING)

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:08.698
(BLOWS)

00:02:09.258 --> 00:02:10.378
(GASPS)

00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:12.178
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

00:02:14.018 --> 00:02:16.618
King Runeard, the dam isn't
strengthening our waters.

00:02:16.778 --> 00:02:18.298
It's hurting the Forest.

00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:19.778
It's cutting off the North...

00:02:19.938 --> 00:02:21.578
Let... Let's not
discuss this here.

00:02:21.738 --> 00:02:24.658
Let's meet on the fjord.
Have tea.

00:02:24.818 --> 00:02:26.458
Find a solution.

00:02:27.698 --> 00:02:29.298
(BREATHING SHAKILY)

00:02:30.258 --> 00:02:31.258
(GASPS)

00:02:37.978 --> 00:02:38.978
No!

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.818
-(ICE CRACKING)
-(GROANING)

00:02:45.258 --> 00:02:46.538
Anna!

00:02:55.658 --> 00:03:00.378
OLAF: Hmm. Which lucky tunnel
do we choose?

00:03:00.538 --> 00:03:02.938
RUNEARD: You see, the dam
will weaken their lands,

00:03:03.018 --> 00:03:04.418
so they will
have to turn to me.

00:03:04.498 --> 00:03:05.938
NORTHULDRA LEADER:
King Runeard, the dam,

00:03:06.058 --> 00:03:07.818
it's hurting the Forest.

00:03:07.898 --> 00:03:09.458
(ANNA AND OLAF GASP)

00:03:12.738 --> 00:03:14.298
Elsa's found it.

00:03:14.458 --> 00:03:15.818
What is it?

00:03:15.978 --> 00:03:17.698
The truth about the past.

00:03:18.938 --> 00:03:20.978
That's my grandfather...

00:03:21.138 --> 00:03:23.978
attacking
the Northuldra leader...

00:03:24.538 --> 00:03:27.058
who wields no weapon.

00:03:28.658 --> 00:03:29.778
(SIGHS SOFTLY)

00:03:29.858 --> 00:03:32.258
The dam
wasn't a gift of peace.

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:34.978
It was a trick.

00:03:35.178 --> 00:03:36.778
But that goes
against everything

00:03:36.858 --> 00:03:38.178
Arendelle stands for.

00:03:38.898 --> 00:03:40.298
It does, doesn't it?

00:03:43.258 --> 00:03:45.458
I know how to free the Forest.

00:03:45.778 --> 00:03:49.218
I know what we have to do
to set things right.

00:03:50.058 --> 00:03:52.098
Why do you say that so sadly?

00:03:53.018 --> 00:03:54.658
We have to break the dam.

00:03:54.818 --> 00:03:56.498
But Arendelle will be flooded.

00:03:57.498 --> 00:04:00.218
That's why everyone
was forced out.

00:04:00.378 --> 00:04:03.298
To protect them
from what has to be done.

00:04:03.658 --> 00:04:05.458
Oh. Oh!

00:04:08.658 --> 00:04:10.178
Are you okay?

00:04:10.338 --> 00:04:12.578
I could really use
a bright side, Olaf.

00:04:13.258 --> 00:04:14.898
Bright side? Um...

00:04:15.618 --> 00:04:17.698
Turtles can breathe
through their butts.

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:21.458
-Huh?
-And I see a way out.

00:04:23.058 --> 00:04:24.898
I knew I could count on you.

00:04:27.538 --> 00:04:28.858
(GROANS)

00:04:29.578 --> 00:04:32.858
Come on, Olaf, Elsa's probably
on her way back right now.

00:04:33.058 --> 00:04:34.258
We can meet her and...

00:04:36.458 --> 00:04:37.458
Olaf?

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:39.578
What's this?

00:04:40.098 --> 00:04:41.298
Are you okay?

00:04:41.538 --> 00:04:43.298
I'm flurrying?

00:04:43.618 --> 00:04:44.698
Wait. No. That's...

00:04:44.818 --> 00:04:46.418
That's not it.

00:04:47.858 --> 00:04:51.098
I'm flurrying away.

00:04:51.778 --> 00:04:54.858
-The magic in me is fading.
-(GASPS)

00:04:54.938 --> 00:04:55.938
What?

00:04:58.138 --> 00:05:00.058
I don't think Elsa's okay.

00:05:00.298 --> 00:05:02.498
-(GASPS)
-I think...

00:05:03.578 --> 00:05:05.738
she may have gone too far.

00:05:06.978 --> 00:05:09.298
No. No.

00:05:09.458 --> 00:05:10.538
OLAF: Anna?

00:05:11.098 --> 00:05:13.098
I'm sorry.

00:05:13.258 --> 00:05:16.338
You're gonna have to do
this next part on your own.

00:05:16.498 --> 00:05:17.978
-Okay?
-Wait.

00:05:18.138 --> 00:05:19.418
Come here.

00:05:19.778 --> 00:05:21.978
-I've got you.
-Oh. (CHUCKLES)

00:05:22.498 --> 00:05:23.898
That's good.

00:05:25.778 --> 00:05:27.178
Hey, Anna?

00:05:27.818 --> 00:05:30.618
I just thought of one thing
that's permanent.

00:05:30.778 --> 00:05:31.938
What's that?

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:34.218
Love.

00:05:35.498 --> 00:05:36.738
Warm hugs?

00:05:37.858 --> 00:05:39.738
-(ANNA SOBBING SOFTLY)
-(WHIMPERS)

00:05:40.378 --> 00:05:43.378
-(SNIFFLES)
-I like warm hugs.

00:05:43.458 --> 00:05:44.898
(ANNA CONTINUES SOBBING)

00:05:48.938 --> 00:05:49.938
(SNIFFLES)

00:05:52.298 --> 00:05:54.058
I love you.

00:06:08.138 --> 00:06:09.378
(WIND WHISTLING)

00:06:10.178 --> 00:06:11.698
(CREATURE CHITTERS)

00:06:15.618 --> 00:06:16.618
(WHINES)

00:06:22.218 --> 00:06:23.738
(WIND WHISTLING)

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:46.698
(BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE)

00:06:47.818 --> 00:06:49.098
(ANNA SNIFFLING)

00:06:49.178 --> 00:06:50.538
(WATER DRIPPING)

00:06:57.218 --> 00:06:58.818
(CRYING)

00:07:00.178 --> 00:07:02.698
Olaf? Elsa?

00:07:04.378 --> 00:07:06.578
What do I do now?

00:07:07.578 --> 00:07:08.938
(CONTINUES CRYING)

00:07:10.578 --> 00:07:13.018
(SINGING)
I've seen dark before

00:07:13.218 --> 00:07:14.858
But not like this

00:07:16.058 --> 00:07:20.738
This is cold, this is empty
This is numb

00:07:22.138 --> 00:07:24.578
The life I knew is over

00:07:24.738 --> 00:07:26.298
The lights are out

00:07:27.018 --> 00:07:28.778
Hello, darkness

00:07:28.978 --> 00:07:31.258
I'm ready to succumb

00:07:33.738 --> 00:07:36.258
I follow you around

00:07:36.418 --> 00:07:38.538
I always have

00:07:38.698 --> 00:07:42.858
But you've gone to a place
I cannot find

00:07:44.378 --> 00:07:47.978
(VOICE BREAKING)
This grief has a gravity

00:07:48.138 --> 00:07:50.458
It pulls me down

00:07:50.538 --> 00:07:52.018
(CONTINUES CRYING)

00:07:54.858 --> 00:07:56.778
But a tiny voice

00:07:57.738 --> 00:08:00.178
Whispers in my mind

00:08:00.258 --> 00:08:01.258
(SNIFFLES)

00:08:02.938 --> 00:08:04.778
You are lost

00:08:05.458 --> 00:08:07.258
Hope is gone

00:08:08.138 --> 00:08:11.738
But you must go on

00:08:13.778 --> 00:08:17.578
And do the next right thing

00:08:18.538 --> 00:08:19.658
(SNIFFLES)

